## Steps to test

`npm start` in the frontend and have the backend docker container up 

1. Create an onboarding request
```
mutation testCreateOnboardingRequest {
  createOnboardingRequest(userInfo: {email: "ENTER YOUR EMAIL", organizationAddress: "123 Main St", organizationName: "Acme Inc", role: "ASP", primaryContact: {name: "John Doe", email: "john.doe@example.com", phone: "555-555-1212"}, onsiteContacts: [{name: "Jane Smith", email: "jane.smith@example.com", phone: "555-555-1212"}, {name: "Bob Johnson", email: "bob.johnson@example.com", phone: "555-555-1212"}]}) {
    onboardingRequest {
      id
      info {
        email
        organizationAddress
        organizationName
        role
        primaryContact {
          name
          email
          phone
        }
        onsiteContacts {
          name
          email
          phone
        }
      }
      dateSubmitted
      status
    }
  }
}
```

2. Copy the ID it returns and approve this onboarding request
```
mutation testApproveOnboardingRequest {
  approveOnboardingRequest(id: "ENTER ID HERE") {
    onboardingRequest {
      id
      info {
        email
        organizationAddress
        organizationName
        role
        primaryContact {
          name
          email
          phone
        }
        onsiteContacts {
          name
          email
          phone
        }
      }
      dateSubmitted
      status
    }
  }
}
```

3. Copy this ID and paste it into `http://localhost:3000/ENTER ID HERE/set-password`

4. Enter a valid password and click `confirm`
5. You should receive an email soon and be redirected to the login page 


